## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Git LFS vs Local Binaries**: In our local repository, the full 1.04MB V3 binary model (`00a8410746f4a0eecbf7e76aaa0565143fc948d0e06aea65e7bcc4ce28a1c660`) is present and passes all 38 backend integrity and reference parity tests. In fresh clones or CI environments lacking Git LFS, this file defaults to a 130-byte pointer stub (`a6f97f...`). We will add an automated artifact guard (`scripts/verify_artifacts.py`) and an immutable manifest (`models/v3/artifact_manifest.json`) to detect this and prevent silent degradation.
> - **Frontend Test Assertions**: 32 of 58 Vitest tests in `frontend/src/test` are currently failing because the test fixtures were written against early UI prototypes (e.g. searching for exact text `"Calibrated Bust Probability"` instead of current `"Calibrated Bust Probability (q95 MAD)"`, or looking for deprecated badge titles). We will align the test assertions with the production components so that `npm test -- --run` achieves 58/58 (100%) pass rate.

